# Estimate-scale applicability and interference interpretation

Additive clarification to ROOT_SCIENTIFIC_REVIEW001 and its labelled numerical
scenario; original source/research/arithmetic records remain intact. No goal,
scientific requirement or historical numerical result is changed.

The source23 and8 values are fitted/extrapolated apparent Vmax summaries.
The signed optical equation y=h−alpha*f is a concentration/signal-rate relation
for the selected contributions. Applying it to fitted summaries requires an
additional mapping assumption: the selected parameter estimates must obey that
linear relation on the same estimate scale. A fit is not automatically a linear
operation on its input signals, and fitting can change an apparent saturation
parameter when interfering rates have different substrate dependence.

