Separating NADH and ferredoxin contributions to an optical signal addresses
readout attribution. It does not by itself establish causal attribution of
that chemistry to the intended polypeptide or complex rather than contaminants
or other contributors. Keep readout decomposition and molecular effect
isolation separately represented; an optical correction is not a molecular
purity or contamination correction.

